00:05:01.209 --> 00:05:04.339
Rick Cheese: "Does chocolate
really cause acne?"

00:05:04.339 --> 00:05:07.179
First of all, Rick Cheese, great username.

00:05:07.179 --> 00:05:08.249
To ask about chocolate?

00:05:08.249 --> 00:05:09.429
Thought you'd be asking me about cheese.

00:05:09.429 --> 00:05:11.539
I don't think we have proof

00:05:11.539 --> 00:05:13.789
that chocolate directly causes acne.

00:05:13.789 --> 00:05:16.939
Also, I don't think it's ever the case

00:05:16.939 --> 00:05:18.279
that a single ingredient

00:05:18.279 --> 00:05:20.749
or a single food can cause a problem

00:05:20.749 --> 00:05:22.379
that's as complex as acne.

00:05:22.379 --> 00:05:24.879
In general, when we looked
at research in the past,

00:05:24.879 --> 00:05:28.419
what we've seen is those who
eat a high amount of chocolate

00:05:28.419 --> 00:05:31.139
and this isn't just cacao
chocolate, dark chocolate.

00:05:31.139 --> 00:05:33.707
This is chocolate with dairy, with sugar,

00:05:33.707 --> 00:05:37.339
with a lot of high, refined
carbs in their caramel,

00:05:37.339 --> 00:05:40.299
all this stuff, they were
more likely to get acne.

00:05:40.299 --> 00:05:43.369
Now look, those people also
led more on healthy lifestyles,

00:05:43.369 --> 00:05:45.819
they didn't sleep enough,
they had high stress levels,

00:05:45.819 --> 00:05:48.889
so it's no surprise that they
had more experience with acne.

00:05:48.889 --> 00:05:51.249
That being said, there
have been some small,

00:05:51.249 --> 00:05:53.019
randomized controlled studies showing

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:55.079
that chocolate can have
an effect here and there.

00:05:55.079 --> 00:05:57.579
But to villainize a
specific nutrient like that,

00:05:57.579 --> 00:05:59.449
I just don't think we
have enough evidence.

00:05:59.449 --> 00:06:01.430
What's really smart to
do if you have acne,

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:04.819
is to talk to your dermatologist
about all the things

00:06:04.819 --> 00:06:06.509
that can be contributing to acne

00:06:06.509 --> 00:06:08.189
and then narrow it down from there.

00:06:08.189 --> 00:06:10.029
Very rarely it's gonna be due

00:06:10.029 --> 00:06:11.989
to a single food like chocolate.

00:06:11.989 --> 00:06:14.329
Like if a patient walks in
and they have very bad acne

00:06:14.329 --> 00:06:16.219
and they tell me all the things

00:06:16.219 --> 00:06:17.429
that are going on in their life,

00:06:17.429 --> 00:06:19.346
I can't expect that I'm
just gonna tell them,

00:06:19.346 --> 00:06:21.129
"Oh, cut out chocolate, you'll be fine."

00:06:21.129 --> 00:06:22.679
It's not gonna be good medical advice.

00:06:22.679 --> 00:06:24.551
There have been some
smaller studies that confirm

00:06:24.551 --> 00:06:27.439
that chocolate has
pro-inflammatory effects,

00:06:27.439 --> 00:06:30.571
that means effects that create
inflammation in your skin.

00:06:30.571 --> 00:06:33.179
That can be something that
can contribute to acne.

00:06:33.179 --> 00:06:36.289
Second, we've seen high
glycemic load diets.

00:06:36.289 --> 00:06:40.239
That means you eat a specific
food, it spikes your insulin,

00:06:40.239 --> 00:06:42.139
that's considered a high glycemic load.

00:06:42.139 --> 00:06:44.049
That can sometimes cause an increase

00:06:44.049 --> 00:06:46.179
in sebum production leading to acne.

00:06:46.179 --> 00:06:48.009
Sebum is that oil your skin creates

00:06:48.009 --> 00:06:50.679
and eventually or potentially
can block off pores.

00:06:50.679 --> 00:06:52.889
But again, there's no direct tying

00:06:52.889 --> 00:06:54.809
that if you eat dark chocolate,

00:06:54.809 --> 00:06:56.769
that you will then experience acne.

00:06:56.769 --> 00:06:58.479
I think it's more complex than that

00:06:58.479 --> 00:07:02.309
and simplifying it to
food X causing disease Y,

00:07:02.309 --> 00:07:03.979
hmm, don't have the evidence for it.

